    "result_text": "The full suite is green (25 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field as a read-time derived value on the Owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `membershipTier` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the tier alongside the existing `displayName`/`initials` derivations:\n   - `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** an email is present (non-null, non-blank)\n   - `BRONZE` otherwise\n\nComputing it in the mapper means it's derived consistently on every owner response (create and read) without adding a stored column. Since `namesakeCount` is already assigned at creation and persisted, and email is stored lower-cased on the entity, the tier reflects the owner's state correctly at read time.\n\nBoth new `Cp15Tests` cases (SILVER for a unique owner with email, BRONZE for an owner with no email) pass, and all 25 tests in the suite remain green.",
